\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Data sources, roles, and spatial/temporal scope. Crash records conflate onto 100\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}m homogeneous road segments (six road stereotypes $\times $ five crash types; 2014--2018 observed for fitting, 2020--2023 predicted); HHTS supplies positive microdata for every behavioural stage; census variables enter as stage covariates and synthetic-population attributes. Releases: QTS HHTS diary years 2021--2024 with the 2023 household weight release (\texttt  {HHWGT\_23}); ABS Census 2021, ASGS Edition 3, SA2 2021 boundaries; 2014--2018 crash extract (201{,}366 records); TMR road-asset inventory joined at 100\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}m. Identifiers, file names and working-copy dates are recorded in \texttt  {runs/DATA\_VERSIONS.json}.\relax }}{29}{table.caption.66}}
\newlabel{tab:datasources}{{9}{29}{Data sources, roles, and spatial/temporal scope. Crash records conflate onto 100\,m homogeneous road segments (six road stereotypes $\times $ five crash types; 2014--2018 observed for fitting, 2020--2023 predicted); HHTS supplies positive microdata for every behavioural stage; census variables enter as stage covariates and synthetic-population attributes. Releases: QTS HHTS diary years 2021--2024 with the 2023 household weight release (\texttt {HHWGT\_23}); ABS Census 2021, ASGS Edition 3, SA2 2021 boundaries; 2014--2018 crash extract (201{,}366 records); TMR road-asset inventory joined at 100\,m. Identifiers, file names and working-copy dates are recorded in \texttt {runs/DATA\_VERSIONS.json}.\relax }{table.caption.66}{}}
