\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Exampville Stages~0--1 comparison. CDAP is fitted on $n=12{,}349$ persons and $k$ is the number of features in the specification. $\Delta \mathrm  {LL}$ is $\mathrm  {E2}-\mathrm  {E1}$, so a negative value means the searched arm fits worse; $\Delta \mathrm  {BIC}/n$ is $\mathrm  {E2}-\mathrm  {E1}$ on the criterion the search optimises, so a negative value favours the searched arm. The Stage-1 rows are mean absolute errors of the per-person tour count against the observed mean, from the corrected re-run (job 27308422); observed means are $0.6125$ work and $1.0669$ non-mandatory tours per person. $^{\dagger }$The searched arm still returned the failure sentinel ($-3.3\times 10^{8}$), so its Stage-1 figures describe a fallback specification rather than a search outcome.\relax }}{32}{table.caption.72}}
\newlabel{tab:exampville_cmp01}{{12}{32}{Exampville Stages~0--1 comparison. CDAP is fitted on $n=12{,}349$ persons and $k$ is the number of features in the specification. $\Delta \mathrm {LL}$ is $\mathrm {E2}-\mathrm {E1}$, so a negative value means the searched arm fits worse; $\Delta \mathrm {BIC}/n$ is $\mathrm {E2}-\mathrm {E1}$ on the criterion the search optimises, so a negative value favours the searched arm. The Stage-1 rows are mean absolute errors of the per-person tour count against the observed mean, from the corrected re-run (job 27308422); observed means are $0.6125$ work and $1.0669$ non-mandatory tours per person. $^{\dagger }$The searched arm still returned the failure sentinel ($-3.3\times 10^{8}$), so its Stage-1 figures describe a fallback specification rather than a search outcome.\relax }{table.caption.72}{}}
\newlabel{tab:exampville_cmp01@cref}{{[table][12][]12}{[1][31][]32}}
