\newlabel{tab:ga_shard2}{{14}{35}{GA Stage-5 variant winners (BIC/n lower is better). Scores are from the run's variant shootout; Appendix~\ref {app:qld-models} reports the final refit of the merged-run genome, which is a different fit with its own LL and $\rho ^2$.\relax }{table.caption.80}{}}
\newlabel{tab:ga_shard2@cref}{{[table][14][]14}{[1][34][]35}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Dead-term audit of the GA winners: every selected term classified by its own coefficient, standard error and $t$-ratio in the refit made with the search switched off (classes defined in the text). \emph  {Dead}: coefficient returns at $0.000$ with $t=0.000$, $p=1.000$ and a finite standard error. \emph  {Clipped}: coefficient on a constraint bound. \emph  {Unmapped}: gene with no estimated parameter. \emph  {Held}: fixed by design (\texttt  {holdfast}), zero standard error by construction, hence not an estimate. Only the live column is a citable effect; a term listed as dead is still part of the published specification, it simply contributes nothing to its fit.\relax }}{35}{table.caption.81}}
\newlabel{tab:ga_dead}{{15}{35}{Dead-term audit of the GA winners: every selected term classified by its own coefficient, standard error and $t$-ratio in the refit made with the search switched off (classes defined in the text). \emph {Dead}: coefficient returns at $0.000$ with $t=0.000$, $p=1.000$ and a finite standard error. \emph {Clipped}: coefficient on a constraint bound. \emph {Unmapped}: gene with no estimated parameter. \emph {Held}: fixed by design (\texttt {holdfast}), zero standard error by construction, hence not an estimate. Only the live column is a citable effect; a term listed as dead is still part of the published specification, it simply contributes nothing to its fit.\relax }{table.caption.81}{}}
\newlabel{tab:ga_dead@cref}{{[table][15][]15}{[1][34][]35}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The non-mandatory searches of \texttt  {qld\_shard3}, recovered from the stdout of a job the scheduler killed for exceeding its memory limit (exit 137). The GA writes a compact summary line every fifth generation and the job died before its history files were flushed, so these summaries are the complete record that survives: six points for mode (generations 0--25) and five for destination (generations 0--20). Top row, BIC/n: mode best-so-far falls $1.7905 \to 1.7891$ and is flat after generation~10, while the population mean stays near $1.795$; destination best-so-far falls $1.0499 \to 1.0399$ while the mean oscillates between $1.06$ and $1.10$ as the population keeps exploring and the incumbent stops improving. Bottom row: features carried by the incumbent (mode $6 \to 5$, destination $18 \to 10$). The late churn at flat best-so-far is the same dead-feature signature as education. Prep accessibilities are healthy (accessibility diagnostics figure, Appendix).\relax }}{35}{figure.caption.82}}
\newlabel{fig:nonmandsalvage}{{4}{35}{The non-mandatory searches of \texttt {qld\_shard3}, recovered from the stdout of a job the scheduler killed for exceeding its memory limit (exit 137). The GA writes a compact summary line every fifth generation and the job died before its history files were flushed, so these summaries are the complete record that survives: six points for mode (generations 0--25) and five for destination (generations 0--20). Top row, BIC/n: mode best-so-far falls $1.7905 \to 1.7891$ and is flat after generation~10, while the population mean stays near $1.795$; destination best-so-far falls $1.0499 \to 1.0399$ while the mean oscillates between $1.06$ and $1.10$ as the population keeps exploring and the incumbent stops improving. Bottom row: features carried by the incumbent (mode $6 \to 5$, destination $18 \to 10$). The late churn at flat best-so-far is the same dead-feature signature as education. Prep accessibilities are healthy (accessibility diagnostics figure, Appendix).\relax }{figure.caption.82}{}}
\newlabel{fig:nonmandsalvage@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][34][]35}}
